  "vector_memory": {
    "semantic_summary": "JsonSerializable is an abstract base class enforcing a contract for objects capable of JSON serialization and deserialization. It manages core metadata like className and uuid, providing recursive logic for converting object properties into a standardized JsonSerializedData structure. It handles primitive types, custom objects with toJsonObject methods, and nested plain objects during serialization. Deserialization populates properties, either directly or by invoking a specific fromJson method on target properties."
  },
